<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Suintila</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 621–631</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Suintila was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 621 to 631. Around 624 he expelled the last Byzantine garrisons from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/isidore-of-seville">Isidore of Seville</a> praised him as the first king to rule the whole peninsula. He was overthrown in 631 by Sisenand with Frankish help, and the Fourth Council of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> later condemned him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/suintila.jpg" alt="Suintila" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Numismática Pliego · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Suintila_Tremis_Barbi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
